From cdb9d4a76a5c85e43ad53505d0bfe556e4770830 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:24:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Committed model switch replaces the recorded
 allocation at the next build

model_in_transaction moved sessions.model/provider but left model_config.model_routing and the
allocation store on the old route, so restore_route resumed the old pin or the next build refused
with 'Exact pinned route cannot fail over'. The receipt transaction now clears the stale record and
writes a one-shot state_meta intent (gateway.route_switch.v1.<target>); prepare_agent_route honours
it only for exactly that session and tuple (replace=True), consuming it by compare-and-delete after
the allocation commits. Rejected/deferred preparations never write it; preparation's route lookups
run as temporary (in-memory) resolutions. No intent: an exact pin still cannot move.
